sson_name"}, {"content": "How Often Do You Go to the Library?", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 4, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "Beginner", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Adverbs of Frequency ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I always go to the library after class.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "An <span class=\"italic\">adverb </span> is a word that can describe a daily activity.  There are different groups of adverbs. One group of adverbs is called <span class=\"strong\"> adverbs of frequency</span>. They tell you how often something happens. Here are some examples:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":\"05\",\"columns\":\"02\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> Adverb</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">How often? </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"always\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"100%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"usually\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"60%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"rarely \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"10%\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"never\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"0%\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": " I usually go to the library to study. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I rarely go to the library before class. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I never go to the library in the morning. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I always go to the library in the morning.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "How often ... ?", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to ask how many times you do something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: How often do you take the bus?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you can use to talk about daily activities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to return", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to take something back to its place of origin", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I have to return my book to the library.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "next time", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a future occasion", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Next time we go to the movies, you can come.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to exercise", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to do physical activity to be healthy", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I exercise every day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Come with me!", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to invite someone to go somewhere with you", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Come with me to the library!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn1le04ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Express information about  daily or weekly routines in a very simple way.", "type": "primary